  "term": "butyrophenone",
  "definition": "Butyrophenone refers to a class of synthetic compounds with a phenyl-1-butanone structure. In mental health contexts, many drugs in this group are antipsychotic medicines used to reduce symptoms such as hallucinations and delusions, often by affecting neurotransmitter activity including dopamine receptor blocking.",
